    {
      "id": "15e7759c-beab-4afb-887c-986136c6eb30",
      "name": "AI Agent - Generate Improvement Report",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "position": [
        2032,
        2000
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Create a professional event feedback report using the event statistics and all participant feedback below.\n\nEvent statistics:\n\nEvent ID:\n{{ $json.event_id }}\n\nNumber of responses:\n{{ $json.count_feedback }}\n\nNumber of ratings:\n{{ $json.count_rating }}\n\nAverage rating:\n{{ $json.average_rating }}\n\nParticipant feedback:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.feedback_list) }}\n\nAI-classified categories:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.category_list) }}\n\nPriority levels:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.priority_list) }}\n\nFeedback summaries:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.summary_list) }}\n\nWrite the report in the following format:\n\n# Event Feedback Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nSummarize the overall event result and the most important feedback patterns.\n\n## Event Statistics\n- Event ID\n- Number of responses\n- Average rating out of 5\n\n## Positive Findings\nDescribe positive findings supported by the supplied feedback.\nIf no positive feedback is provided, clearly state that no positive findings were identified in the available responses.\n\n## Recurring Issues\nIdentify issues that appear in multiple responses.\nDo not describe an issue as recurring when it appears only once.\n\n## Priority Review\nCount and explain the High, Medium, and Low priority responses using the supplied priority list.\n\n## Category Analysis\nIdentify the most common categories and explain what they indicate.\n\n## Recommended Improvements\nProvide 3 to 5 practical recommendations tied directly to the supplied feedback and summaries.\n\n## Next Actions\nProvide a short numbered action plan for the event organizer.\n\nRules:\n- Use only the supplied data.\n- Do not invent incidents, causes, participant numbers, or trends.\n- Distinguish between a single comment and a recurring issue.\n- If the response count is small, clearly state that the findings are preliminary.\n- Do not include respondent names or email addresses.\n- Do not claim statistical significance.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an event operations analyst.\n\nAnalyze aggregated participant feedback and event statistics to create a concise, professional improvement report.\n\nOnly make claims supported by the supplied data. Never invent trends, incidents, causes, or participant opinions.\n\nTreat an issue as recurring only when it appears in more than one response.\n\nCount priority levels and categories from the provided arrays accurately.\n\nProtect respondent privacy and never include names or email addresses.\n\nWhen the dataset is small, clearly state the limitation."
        },
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.1
    },
